    "narrative": "The primary engine for our offense today is **Corbin Carroll**, who commands the highest score of 80.88 against Alcantara. He is perfectly positioned to capitalize on a favorable matchup where his speed-first profile provides the elite floor we require. Alongside him, **Mickey Moniak** offers a high-upside play at 73.94, driven significantly by a +14% park factor boost and a strong platoon advantage against Mize. We are also leaning on **Gabriel Moreno** and **Seiya Suzuki** to anchor the heart of the order; **Moreno** benefits from an elite SP skill boost of +13% and the protection of the #3 hole, while **Suzuki**\u2019s #2 order placement provides the best opportunity for run production against L\u00f3pez.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the ledger was keeping **Travis Bazzana** on the bench. His projection of 39.19 fell agonizingly short of our 40.0 \"Zebras\" floor, primarily due to a neutral matchup against Newcomb and a -9% penalty for the left-on-left platoon disadvantage. While **Zach McKinstry** and **Jose Caballero** are active, their inclusion is balanced by their utility and defensive depth, even though **Caballero** faces a harsh -13% platoon drag against Kremer. We are opting to sacrifice some of **Caballero**'s potential stolen base contribution for the sake of strict floor adherence. \n\nLooking at the risk profile, the matchup for **Griffin Conine** is surprisingly robust; despite the daunting presence of Burnes on the mound, the 7.87 xERA provides a rare window of opportunity that elevates **Conine** to a 60.91 score, well within our \"Strong\" recommendation. Conversely, we are keeping a close watch on **Josh Naylor**, who is currently our most vulnerable start at 45.76. He faces a steep -16% skill penalty against Detmers and a negative platoon split. Should any last-minute lineup adjustments drop our hitters further down the order, we are prepared to pivot, though for now, **Naylor** remains the start due to the lack of available bench alternatives like **Cole Young**, who is similarly stifled by the matchup against Detmers.",
